So switch over to the clone and the recovery is just the two steps that matter: prove data flows with one doc, then refill. On the clone:

bash
AUTH='admin:ksdjhfskjdhl'; OS=https://localhost:9200
SRC=https://SOURCE_IP:9200          # the prod box's IP
c(){ curl -sk -u "$AUTH" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' "$OS/$@"; }

# 1. one-doc test — this prints the real error if the prereqs are missing
c -XPOST '_reindex' -d "{
  \"source\":{\"remote\":{\"host\":\"$SRC\",\"username\":\"admin\",\"password\":\"ksdjhfskjdhl\"},
    \"index\":\"gladsaxe-2026.10\",\"size\":1,\"max_docs\":1},
  \"dest\":{\"index\":\"zz-test\"}}"

If that returns "created":1, the link works — delete the probe (c -XDELETE zz-test -o /dev/null) and run the refill:

bash
# 2. refill the three emptied indices (no drop, reindex auto-creates mappings)
for i in gladsaxe-2026.08 gladsaxe-2026.09 gladsaxe-2026.10; do
  echo "=== $i ==="
  c -XPOST "_reindex?wait_for_completion=false&slices=auto" -d "{
    \"source\":{\"remote\":{\"host\":\"$SRC\",\"username\":\"admin\",\"password\":\"ksdjhfskjdhl\",
      \"socket_timeout\":\"5m\"},\"index\":\"$i\",\"size\":2000},
    \"dest\":{\"index\":\"$i\"}}"
  echo
done

c '_tasks?actions=*reindex&detailed' | python3 -m json.tool   # watch progress
